From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: the screen DC's bitmap survives a program deleting it

GetCurrentObject(OBJ_BITMAP) of a screen (display) DC gives the bitmap
every display DC of the process shares (get_display_bitmap), and
DeleteObject took it: marked deleted while selected, GetDIBits on any screen
DC's bitmap failed from then on. TightVNC's desktop server does exactly that
-- Screen::getBMI asks GetDIBits for the screen's format, then deletes the
bitmap and the DC -- so it ended at its second look ("Can't get a DIBits")
and a VNC viewer never got a picture. On Windows that bitmap is a system
object, which DeleteObject leaves alone; now it is one here too (and stops
being one only when the display's size changes and it is replaced).

Gate: test/displaybitmap-gate.sh. Mutant SG_MUTANT_DISPLAY_BITMAP_DELETABLE.
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -2528,9 +2528,21 @@
     pthread_mutex_lock( &display_dc_lock );
     if (!EqualRect( &old_virtual_rect, &virtual_rect ))
     {
-        if (hbitmap) NtGdiDeleteObjectApp( hbitmap );
+        /* Stained Glass OS (9627): the display DCs' bitmap is the system's,
+         * as on Windows: a program that deletes what GetCurrentObject(OBJ_BITMAP)
+         * gave it for a screen DC (TightVNC's Screen::getBMI does) must not
+         * break every screen DC after it -- GetDIBits failed on it from then
+         * on, and TightVNC's desktop server ended */
+        if (hbitmap)
+        {
+            make_gdi_object_system( hbitmap, FALSE );
+            NtGdiDeleteObjectApp( hbitmap );
+        }
         hbitmap = NtGdiCreateBitmap( virtual_rect.right - virtual_rect.left,
                                      virtual_rect.bottom - virtual_rect.top, 1, 32, NULL );
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_DISPLAY_BITMAP_DELETABLE
+        if (hbitmap) make_gdi_object_system( hbitmap, TRUE );
+#endif
         old_virtual_rect = virtual_rect;
     }
     ret = hbitmap;
